fix crossfade

A natural crossfade can override a manual track selection
---------------------------------------------------------
Reported 2026-11-16. Symptoms when clicking a track while the current one is
inside its crossfade window:

- the next track in the queue plays instead of the clicked one; clicking the
  clicked row again plays the right one;
- the lyrics panel shows the previous/next track's lyrics;
- the seek bar's length/position keep changing with the other track.

Cause, in order:

1. app.cpp runs maybe_start_crossfade() before the pending-play block.
   maybe_start_crossfade() does not check pending_manual_play /
   pending_play_url, so a speculative fade starts after a click.
2. adopt_fade_track() (app_playback.cpp:711) overwrites current_track_id,
   title, artist and the lyrics target with the fade target -- which is the
   next queue row -- and stores the clicked track as crossfade_from_track.
3. The EOF handler's `g_cf.active` branch (app_playback.cpp:1280) promotes the
   fade target and returns before the pending-manual-play guard below it.
4. The "start" handler's was_manual branch assumes the UI already shows the
   clicked track and never restores the metadata adopt_fade_track clobbered.
5. Lyrics intentionally show the outgoing track until fade progress >= 0.5
   (ui_lyrics.cpp:315); the seek bar switches to crossfade_position /
   crossfade_duration at 0.5 (ui_bottom.cpp:148). Both then describe the wrong
   track.

Fix plan:

1. maybe_start_crossfade(): return early while pending_manual_play or
   pending_play_url is set -- a manual pick always beats a speculative fade.
2. The EOF g_cf.active branch: if a manual play is pending, do not promote the
   fade target; stop the helper and let the manual resolve take over.
3. On the "start" event with was_manual, re-assert title/artist/thumbnail/ids
   from the pending_* fields and refresh lyrics_requested_id.

Repro: crossfade duration > 0, click a track during the last seconds of the
current one; the next queue row plays. Setting crossfade to 0 should mask it.
